(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Writing Mathematics in Notebooks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ff446e70-6c9f-4b21-bb6f-9b5bf81a6562"],

Cell["MathNotebook Tutorial", "Author",ExpressionUUID->"b49fa865-8806-4eaf-bae5-b2a12d95841a"],

Cell["\<\
How to write a mathematics paper in a Wolfram notebook: journal stylesheets, \
live referencing, and conversion between LaTeX source and native typeset \
math. Whether the mathematics is written as LaTeX or as built-in typeset math \
is your choice throughout \[LongDash] the palette only moves a selection from \
one to the other.\
\>", "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"a397541c-a5f2-40c2-b0a2-410b0a98abf4"],

Cell["Getting Started", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"10c122fe-16a5-4768-a4ae-68541ea9ca1c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "After installing the paclet, restart the front end so that ",
 StyleBox["Palettes \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the stylesheet menu appear."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"458853d3-c54b-47e5-84b7-edbafd6adde3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Give a notebook a journal style with ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Stylesheet \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", or the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Apply stylesheet",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu; ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in that menu takes it back."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ab2093c3-7d7f-4138-891f-c16fa18fdd7a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Style the opening cells ",
 StyleBox["Title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then write in ",
 StyleBox["Section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"078340e8-8499-46a9-ab41-01b625ca1b5f"],

Cell["\<\
Every palette button acts on the notebook you were last editing, and on its \
current selection.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e268e2a9-4476-4c49-9ab3-45f3790d1722"],

Cell["\<\
The journal stylesheets are light-only; applying one from the palette also \
sets the notebook to light mode, so printed and exported output matches the \
screen.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"388ab7d9-5210-4f5a-aa96-e0d2b1e10546"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Update from cloud",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", in the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Setup",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group, asks the Wolfram Cloud which version is published and installs it \
only when it is newer than the one you have \[LongDash] so checking costs a \
line of text, not a download. It then rebuilds the front end menus and \
reopens the palette, which makes the new palette, stylesheets and tutorial \
live immediately."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6dbc5eb9-3c26-48fc-bc0c-507220abbd70"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It always says which of three things happened: updated, with the old and \
new version numbers; already current; or the cloud could not be reached. \
Kernel code from the new version loads after ",
 StyleBox["Evaluation \[RightArrow] Quit Kernel",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the button will not quit the kernel out from under your \
session."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"74898b13-d10d-4c7f-982d-03fd98281f4e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A copy loaded from a development directory shadows anything installed from \
the cloud, so the button reports that and downloads nothing. The same check \
from code: ",
 StyleBox["UpdateMathNotebook[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fa91cde3-bd32-4042-9a4c-08116146d94e"],

Cell["Referencing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c29f9822-5b99-4b55-b672-16034b45741b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select a numbered cell \[LongDash] an equation, a theorem, a section, a \
numbered item \[LongDash] and press ",
 StyleBox["Copy reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then paste into your text."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a0626226-1e25-49bf-9e5e-e788abde1434"],

Cell["\<\
The pasted reference is a live button showing the current number, so \
reordering cells renumbers every reference to them.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f0c3e840-9189-46a9-b7a5-275ff99ebf3a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Clicking a reference jumps to its target; ",
 StyleBox["\[UpArrow] Go back",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns to where you clicked from."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"005431c3-fbdc-4cfc-ac1a-1921a81ac51b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Tag cell",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " names a cell, and ",
 StyleBox["Insert citation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " inserts a red bracketed link to that name \[LongDash] the two together \
give a bibliography: style each entry ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", tag it, cite it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b96a903e-cac6-47b2-ab0a-7d1c6826af04"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A citation to a numbered environment shows its number instead of its tag: \
tag a theorem, cite it, and the citation reads ",
 StyleBox["Theorem 1.1",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] renumbering itself when cells move, in the exported PDF as on \
screen. A tag no cell carries yet keeps its brackets, so a citation written \
before its target is still readable."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"da3e325c-b6f4-4f2a-b45b-264139a3a82d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tagging a ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell also labels it: the entry shows its tag in brackets in the margin, \
which is exactly what a citation to it reads, so the bibliography and the \
body agree without your typing either."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"73474266-4280-48b9-aa38-49dc9d021732"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a bibliography tagged before that was true \[LongDash] or tagged \
through the Cell Tags dialog rather than the palette \[LongDash] ",
 StyleBox["LabelReferences[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " labels every entry of a notebook at once, and clears the label of an entry \
whose tag you removed."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4f4087e4-9699-49ea-a5bd-1a845edf793d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Existing tags are listed under ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Cell Tags",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a6e112d3-5afc-45d3-a368-e412ecfb7ede"],

Cell["\<\
The theorem below and the equation after it are practice targets: select \
either one and copy a reference to it.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9656c9ac-6cf0-4345-835b-5fe3e2821a21"],

Cell["The exponential map is surjective onto the unit circle.", "Theorem",ExpressionUUID->"8f75ee13-4f1c-43f1-9a3e-01bd34c5b6fd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", "\[Pi]"}]], "+", "1", "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"a9aa2833-60aa-\
4340-a4d3-5d976738bbaf"],

Cell["Stylesheets", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"12d01e6c-2380-4639-b730-a4490dd3d8da"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Four templates: ",
 StyleBox["AMSArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (amsart, Palatino), ",
 StyleBox["ArXivArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (article, Latin Modern), ",
 StyleBox["SpringerJournal",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["RevTeXAPS",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (Times)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0fe966ae-65a5-42ca-b9eb-db85eba1a6b8"],

Cell["\<\
All four define the same style names, so switching between them is instant \
and changes nothing but the typography.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"871755f4-816b-448c-8e24-dde1dac26580"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PlainArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a fifth sheet and not a template: it is the notebook's own typography \
with the paper structure added, and it is what an imported paper opens on \
when its \\documentclass names no journal above."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e241f173-aa9c-43f9-b196-69ec995030ca"],

Cell["\<\
Theorem, Lemma, Proposition, Corollary, Conjecture, Claim, Definition, \
Example, Construction, Remark, Question, and Observation share a single \
counter that resets at each section, exactly as in LaTeX; numbered equations \
count continuously through the document.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"63e6f7de-197a-4006-8f0e-6d8cee597d2c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Insert environments from the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Insert environment",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu, or with the ",
 StyleBox["Proof",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["Equation (n)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " buttons."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ed183c3c-a86a-4f73-92c9-f69f63c4aac3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern and TeX Gyre are LaTeX fonts, not system fonts: press ",
 StyleBox["Install LaTeX fonts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " once to copy them out of a local TeX distribution (",
 ButtonBox["tug.org/texlive",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 ") into your user font directory, then restart the front end. They are \
installed for the whole machine, not inside Mathematica, so any application \
can use them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"078ad9d7-8dcc-4f44-baca-4dfa076bc090"],

Cell["Reading and Writing Comfortably", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"27bc51f9-1016-47de-ba6b-1feaca23f03d"],

Cell["\<\
Each palette group folds: click its opener or its name to collapse it, so \
only the buttons you are using take up room. The palette remembers which \
groups are open across front end restarts.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"98c55386-8f0d-4ff4-aded-11595dcb0e39"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["Document view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group holds two sliders and a reset. Like every other palette control they \
act on the notebook you were last editing, so leave the palette open beside \
your paper and drag while you read it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a3837ab2-02e7-42be-bc1b-095b7c306262"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Text size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sets the size of ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and scales the rest of the prose with it \[LongDash] the title, the \
headings, the abstract, the theorem environments, proofs, bibliography \
entries, and both kinds of list \[LongDash] so the document keeps its \
proportions instead of one style growing alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"29a6bee1-aede-451f-b9d4-5a9c22200234"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " does the same for displayed equations and their numbers, independently of \
the prose \[LongDash] the usual reason to reach for it is an equation left \
too small to read beside text you have just enlarged."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5cb028ce-78e7-4c83-8c25-bb7f5fad1aab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both set real font sizes, so they reach the exported PDF. ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Magnification",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a different thing entirely \[LongDash] it zooms the screen and never \
changes print."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"51cc7734-c0b8-4635-ab44-3193fb46e313"],

Cell["\<\
The settings are stored in the notebook itself, so they survive saving and \
reopening and travel with the file to a coauthor.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"067c55a9-1cd4-44aa-83cc-f8911d2f541c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reset view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns the notebook to its stylesheet defaults and leaves no trace of the \
overrides; applying a stylesheet clears them too, since the new sheet \
replaces them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0a8772e5-6e77-4c5c-902e-d8dddc29baaa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX cells are images and cannot inherit a style, so ",
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " re-renders each of them through LaTeX at the new size, from the TeX the \
cell stores."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e5ff2618-a1ba-4d33-80ac-f04d12264522"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same from code, on any notebook: ",
 StyleBox["SetDocumentFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["SetMathFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] each takes ",
 StyleBox["Automatic",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop its own override \[LongDash] and ",
 StyleBox["ResetDocumentView[nb]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop all of them. They work on a notebook still using ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " too."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"630b25ca-0628-466c-ae45-71aefd213ff7"],

Cell["Math Input Shortcuts", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e8605d00-62b4-4f74-abd1-7b6194ceba2c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " inline math in text, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " exits."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4ef7e09e-dbc4-4866-8ef4-7dcaba31da22"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+/",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fraction, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+2",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " square root."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ac0e2520-0642-440f-bbdb-a275040eefcd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+^",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " superscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+_",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " subscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+%",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " switches between them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6a0d4ab2-0ef2-4048-ade1-7ad49e980475"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["name",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " enters symbols: ",
 StyleBox["a",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Alpha], ",
 StyleBox["el",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Element], ",
 StyleBox["->",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Rule]."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c4da17bb-ec57-4a0b-8563-69bca92abdb2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " shows the cell expression (",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " on Windows)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"48c0d0a2-c295-492c-b5cb-4903699380b4"],

Cell["Working with Cells", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"66853ae6-53ff-48e6-a377-53e8c6be78f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Click a cell bracket to select the cell; drag across brackets to select \
several; ",
 StyleBox["Delete",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " removes them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"31033be9-dd2a-4be4-8abc-e0836df8c3b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " extends the selection outward; repeat to reach the whole cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"75a1ebee-1b79-4e24-a884-0c9537e2ed87"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["5",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["7",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " restyle a cell: Title, Section, Subsection, Text, Input."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"abf5d98c-ff90-4957-9fe2-4af61e88c07b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+D",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " divides a cell at the cursor; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+M",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " merges selected cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"015b2fc4-e8f6-4015-a04d-9e99a7b84f2b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " groups selected cells; ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ungroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d6493343-f64d-4334-9026-c3221e854d0a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Double-click a group bracket to close or open the group; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+{",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+}",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " open and close all subgroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"97245e73-9c59-4a85-bb51-98c945b4946d"],

Cell["\<\
Double-click a closed group's remaining bracket to reopen it; use Cell \
\[RightArrow] Delete All Output before sharing a notebook.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fac45a7d-d7ca-40b9-865d-00042b6c885e"],

Cell["LaTeX Conversion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f094ced4-7ea2-45f2-b60a-62b749570b9d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three palette groups convert, and the heading of each says what it moves \
between: ",
 StyleBox["Whole paper (LaTeX)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is the route for a paper, ",
 StyleBox["Selection: LaTeX \[LeftRightArrow] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Selection: math \[LeftRightArrow] MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " act on the cells you have selected. The buttons are named by the verb \
alone \[LongDash] hover one for a sentence on what it does."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1533f155-2ee9-498a-823b-ac6811363992"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Import .tex file\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reads a whole paper into a new notebook: ",
 StyleBox["\\section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the theorem-like environments the preamble declares become cells of \
the matching style, mathematics is typeset, ",
 StyleBox["\\label",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes a cell tag, and ",
 StyleBox["\\ref",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\cite",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become live links. Anything it does not convert is carried verbatim, so \
what it cannot read it also does not damage."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fc473655-5afb-4cd4-9372-6609558a32dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The front matter comes with it: ",
 StyleBox["\\title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\date",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become Title, Author and Date cells you can edit \[LongDash] the edit \
reaches the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] and an ",
 StyleBox["abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes Abstract cells, headed once however many paragraphs it runs to. ",
 StyleBox["\\maketitle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " has no content of its own, so it stays as text beside ",
 StyleBox["\\sloppy",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\tableofcontents",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d9555e87-11cc-4220-aaff-d051fc562b51"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["itemize",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["enumerate",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["description",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become Item and ItemNumbered cells, one per ",
 StyleBox["\\item",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", nesting into Subitem and Subsubitem. Each list restarts its numbering as \
LaTeX does, an ",
 StyleBox["\\item[label]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " prints the label instead of the number, and a second paragraph of one item \
becomes an ItemParagraph cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7d228b95-1922-4615-b142-31a3bfcb79df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["figure",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes its caption plus an ",
 StyleBox["Input",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell holding the code that draws the picture \[LongDash] an ",
 StyleBox["Import",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of the file the paper shipped, which you replace with the Wolfram code \
that generates it. Evaluate the cell and the figure is live; the picture's \
own markup, TikZ included, still goes back into the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " untouched, so the generating code stays the notebook's alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"12db1167-3039-4b1e-a6da-1a7894721025"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bibliography comes in whichever way the paper writes it. A ",
 StyleBox["thebibliography",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes one Reference cell per ",
 StyleBox["\\bibitem",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", each showing its key in brackets exactly as the citations to it read, and \
each is yours to edit \[LongDash] the edit reaches the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Entries pulled from a ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become the same cells, but there the ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " stays the source of truth: only the ",
 StyleBox["\\bibliography",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " commands go back out, so edit the ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and re-import. A declared ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that is not beside the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is reported rather than passed over in silence."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fffa157e-82c1-4918-a0ae-e71b3276029c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Export to .tex\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " writes the whole notebook back out as a paper. An imported one comes back \
as the source it was read from, edits and all; a notebook you wrote here \
comes out as LaTeX built from its styles. This is the export route \
\[LongDash] the two buttons below are for a handful of cells, not for a \
submission."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bd6d9500-7f06-46ff-bb9c-5cfbb35d51ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Export submission\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " writes the paper into a directory instead of into a file, and puts \
everything it needs to compile beside it: each figure file the ",
 StyleBox["\\includegraphics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " commands name, each ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " the preamble declares, and \[LongDash] where a local ",
 StyleBox["pdflatex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is found \[LongDash] the ",
 StyleBox[".bbl",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", which arXiv needs because it runs LaTeX but does not run BibTeX. That \
directory is the upload. A ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " on its own names files that stayed behind and compiles nowhere but the \
paper's original directory, which is the whole reason this button exists \
beside the one above."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2a79ba7c-33c7-4f64-8e03-585b20a42a8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nothing arXiv rejects goes into it: no ",
 StyleBox[".aux",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox[".log",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and no compiled PDF \[LongDash] the LaTeX run happens in a scratch copy \
and only the ",
 StyleBox[".bbl",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " comes back. A file the paper names that is not on disk is reported by \
name, never quietly left out and never re-rendered from the notebook: the \
format and size the ",
 StyleBox["\\includegraphics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " assumes are not recoverable, and guessing them would be guessing at how \
you compile."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0d2b21ea-109a-474b-aef7-51ffecfac52f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Typeset",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reads the selected cells as LaTeX and replaces the mathematics in them \
with editable typeset math; ",
 StyleBox["Show source",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " turns it back into LaTeX you can read or paste elsewhere. With nothing \
selected, the whole notebook."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6d877804-512e-47cf-96dc-0197128e8168"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Typeset",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " parses inline ",
 StyleBox["$\[Ellipsis]$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\(\[Ellipsis]\\)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and displayed ",
 StyleBox["$$\[Ellipsis]$$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\[\[Ellipsis]\\]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "; the starred forms stay unnumbered, the unstarred ones become numbered \
equations."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ff69e0b4-c267-48b0-a95c-c6bd59b5a626"],

Cell["\<\
A display environment written inside a paragraph, with prose on the lines \
around it, is lifted out into its own equation cell and the prose stays in \
Text cells on either side.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"550e3463-869c-4294-b67c-6bfc533135b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " environment becomes a grid aligned on its ",
 StyleBox["&",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", so it stays editable as one equation cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b16d831f-86c1-4584-807a-a646490f2a8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each converted cell keeps its original TeX, so ",
 StyleBox["Show source",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gives back what you typed rather than a re-serialization of the boxes. \
Anything the parser cannot read is left untouched."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"14ce344b-3d26-458f-9f27-b1261ba38468"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Input, Code, and Output cells are skipped, so ",
 StyleBox["$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in code is safe."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"db16de46-d465-4d7b-92d3-82caa5116844"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same from code, on any notebook: ",
 StyleBox["ImportLaTeXDocument[\"paper.tex\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["ExportLaTeXDocument[nb, \"paper.tex\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["ExportLaTeXBundle[nb, \"directory\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for the whole paper, ",
 StyleBox["ConvertLaTeXCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["ConvertMathCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for a selection."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4fb7e4c6-697c-47df-baa5-0588786cb372"],

Cell["MaTeX", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f803d9d6-5dc8-47c8-9037-d638894b5366"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX (",
 ButtonBox["github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"],
 ") is optional, and needs a TeX distribution and Ghostscript. It is used \
only by the ",
 StyleBox["Selection: math \[LeftRightArrow] MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group; referencing, stylesheets, and LaTeX conversion do not."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2c5cec93-ef0c-4dfe-95af-95e937716c7a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use it when an equation has to come out of real LaTeX \[LongDash] macros, \
",
 StyleBox["tikz-cd",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " diagrams, exact journal metrics."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"12380d0e-d4bb-4fdb-ab8a-e4a5debaa978"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Install MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " installs the paclet and points it at the local ",
 StyleBox["pdflatex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["gs",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f83f289b-053a-42fd-8b09-4883171b5cc5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Render",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sends the selected display equations through LaTeX, at whatever size ",
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is showing mathematics at; ",
 StyleBox["Restore",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gives back editable typeset math from the TeX stored in each cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e9aabddd-81ee-45d1-a90e-1698e89bdae0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MaTeX preferences",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " opens your ",
 StyleBox["init.m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in the front end \[LongDash] deliberately not through the system handler \
for ",
 StyleBox[".m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " files. Set the preamble, the magnification, and ",
 StyleBox["$useMaTeXQ = True",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to route TeX typed into a notebook through LaTeX instead of the built-in \
parser."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"16511183-20ca-4484-b8fc-83068e9761e1"],

Cell["\<\
MaTeX cells are images: convert them back before editing, and keep rendering \
for last.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6684182e-5a8a-4234-9426-27f1a7797471"],

Cell["Best Practices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"044262e8-679e-4bf8-97d7-0661b3374cfb"],

Cell["\<\
One environment per cell, inserted from the palette, keeps the styles and \
counters consistent.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b6111944-ff7b-41a5-be5a-77c1d35adbf8"],

Cell["\<\
Tag cells as you write them; tagging a theorem after fifty pages means \
finding it again.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"904546c9-278e-4e0c-87b6-ad064543820b"],

Cell["\<\
Do not strip cell tagging rules: they hold the TeX source that makes the \
round trip lossless.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f21b73b3-6e1e-4175-8482-283b0a706f5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Export to .tex\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " at submission time, not continuously \[LongDash] the notebook is the \
source. Use ",
 StyleBox["Export submission\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " when the destination is arXiv: a ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " alone is not a submission."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"370ad08e-2fa0-4f7f-8e58-34238465f9af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before sharing: ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Delete All Output",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["Restore",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " the MaTeX cells so a coauthor can edit them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a2aae8f2-5f57-45b1-9e1d-a6bf07493f52"],

Cell["Credits", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f54d395d-4cb1-406b-a3fa-82b41db3b004"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The referencing scheme and the MaTeX integration are originally due to Nik \
Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"],
 "; this paclet packages and extends that work."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"418dd879-867a-484f-871f-fe800f41a023"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nik Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["https://github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[murzin]"]],
 CellTags->"murzin",ExpressionUUID->"0f9f17ad-af1d-4bf1-85c3-9939ccc91b80"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Szabolcs Horvat, MaTeX: LaTeX labels in Mathematica, ",
 ButtonBox["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[matex]"]],
 CellTags->"matex",ExpressionUUID->"91550b18-f013-4f1f-b836-604897d5058a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "TeX Live, ",
 ButtonBox["https://tug.org/texlive/",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 " \[LongDash] on macOS, MacTeX, ",
 ButtonBox["https://tug.org/mactex/",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/mactex/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/mactex/"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[texlive]"]],
 CellTags->"texlive",ExpressionUUID->"2c8df5aa-718d-4bca-9c69-51580edb3a03"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern, ",
 ButtonBox["https://ctan.org/pkg/lm",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://ctan.org/pkg/lm"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://ctan.org/pkg/lm"],
 " and TeX Gyre, ",
 ButtonBox["https://ctan.org/pkg/tex-gyre",
